msgid ""
"History Panel in DataLab, the open-source scientific data analysis and "
"visualization platform"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"DataLab, history, record, replay, session, scientific, data, analysis, "
"visualization, platform"
msgstr ""

msgid "History Panel"
msgstr ""

msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The \"History Panel\" records the sequence of actions performed by the "
"user on signals and images, organized into **sessions**. Each session is "
"a chronological list of either:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**UI actions** (creating a new signal, removing selected objects, saving "
"the workspace to HDF5, ...), or"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**computations** (FFT, average, Gaussian fit, ...) dispatched through the"
" Sigima processor."
msgstr ""

msgid "A recorded session can be:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Replayed**, either entirely or starting from a selected action, to "
"reproduce the exact same sequence on the current workspace;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Restored to a given selection state** without re-executing anything, to"
" quickly jump back to a previous working context;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Saved to a standalone history file** (``.dlhist``) or **embedded in the"
" workspace** when saving to HDF5, so that the full processing chain "
"travels with the data."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The History Panel after recording a representative session: create three "
"signals (Voigt, Lorentzian, Lorentzian), remove one of them, create a "
"Gaussian signal, compute the average, add Gaussian noise to the result "
"and run a Gaussian fit."
msgstr ""

msgid "Toolbar"
msgstr ""

msgid "The toolbar at the top of the panel exposes the following actions:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"|record| **Record mode**: toggle the recording of new actions. When off, "
"no new entry is added to the history (existing sessions are preserved)."
msgstr ""

msgid "record"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"|replay| **Replay**: replay the selected action (or the whole session if "
"a session row is selected) without changing the current workspace "
"selection beforehand."
msgstr ""

msgid "replay"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"|restore_selection| **Restore selection**: only re-select the objects "
"that were selected when the action was originally executed; no "
"computation is re-run."
msgstr ""

msgid "restore_selection"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"|restore_and_replay| **Restore selection and replay**: combine the two "
"previous actions -- restore the selection first, then replay."
msgstr ""

msgid "restore_and_replay"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"|edit_mode| **Edit mode**: when on, replaying a computation opens the "
"parameters dialog so the user can tweak the parameters before re-running."
msgstr ""

msgid "edit_mode"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"|delete| **Delete**: remove the selected actions or sessions from the "
"history."
msgstr ""

msgid "delete"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Double-clicking on an action row in the tree is equivalent to \"Restore "
"selection and replay\"."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tree view"
msgstr ""

msgid "The tree view organizes recorded actions into expandable sessions:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each top-level row is a **session**, automatically created when recording"
" is enabled and a new application context is started."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each child row is an **action**, with its title, date/time and a "
"description summarising the parameters (for computations) or the call "
"(for UI actions)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The selection of one or several rows drives which actions are targeted by"
" the toolbar buttons."
msgstr ""

msgid "Session replay across workspaces"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A full session can be replayed on a workspace that no longer contains the"
" objects originally referenced by the recorded actions -- typically after"
" loading a saved session into a fresh workspace. In that case, the panel "
"**remaps the recorded object identifiers** to the newly-created ones on "
"the fly:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"UI actions creating new objects (e.g. *New signal*) enqueue the freshly "
"created identifiers;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"subsequent computations claim the identifiers they need from that queue, "
"in the same order as the original recording;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"UI actions removing objects keep the queue in sync with the live "
"workspace contents, so chained creation/removal sequences replay "
"correctly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This makes it possible, for instance, to record a full processing chain "
"on one dataset, save it, then re-apply the exact same chain on a "
"different but structurally identical input."
msgstr ""

msgid "Persistence"
msgstr ""

msgid "The history can be persisted in two complementary ways:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Embedded in the workspace**: when the workspace is saved to HDF5 "
"(``File > Save to HDF5 file``), the History Panel content is "
"automatically saved alongside the signals and images. Reloading the "
"workspace restores the recorded sessions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Standalone history file**: the panel can also be serialised to a "
"dedicated ``.dlhist`` file, which is convenient to share or version a "
"processing chain independently of the data it was applied to."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Replaying a session that depends on external files (e.g. opening a "
"dataset from disk) will only succeed if those files are still available "
"at the same locations as when the session was recorded."
msgstr ""

